  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1100 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nA strong southern ridge will bring hot and humid conditions\nthrough the week. Shower and storm chances will be at their lowest\nTuesday, mostly less than 30 percent. But, even with low pops, \nany storms could be impactful with torrential rainfall and gusty \nwinds. \n\nThe ridge may weaken slightly with increased storm coverage\nWednesday and Thursday, but just how much the ridge weakens is \nuncertain. Unfortunately, it looks like the ridge will pump up even\nstronger next weekend, perhaps sending actual temps toward 100 \ndegrees in some areas. Although it looks like we can hold off on \nheat headlines for Monday, we will almost certainly need to \nhighlight the heat danger at some point through the coming week \ninto next weekend. Most days will reach level 3 out of 4 which is \ncalled \"Major\". See heat.gov for more information.",
